#import(../prelude/measure.will)

% =============================================================================
% WFC.will — wave function collapse on the ∃_ρ + bias surface (TODO_0298).
% =============================================================================
%
% A 1D "beach" of 4 cells over tiles {sea, coast, land}, priors 2:1:2,
% with the classic constraint sea–land never adjacent. This is the P3
% surface the P1 version hand-compiled: each cell's wave IS the graded
% existential —
%
%   spawn: mk C -o { exists T: tile_t @w. tile C T }.
%
% suspended under plain settle (D4 opt-in), opened and drawn by the
% decimation driver (calc.collapse; interactively: the shell's collapse
% mode, npm run shell:will -- calculus/will/game/WFC.will). Constraint
% propagation is the BIAS DISCIPLINE (M8): a collapsed cell derives
% `!bias E T' 0` against its neighbor's still-open wave evar, and the
% posterior renormalizes automatically — no dom bitmask, no per-mask
% woplus weight table. (The old mask-shrinking propagation shape lives
% on as the D16 strict-measure pin in tests/engine/will-wfc.test.js.)
%
% Decimation order (M5, min entropy): a biased wave has fewer live
% members than an open one, so propagate-then-collapse-tightest-first
% IS the draw policy. Contradiction (zero posterior mass) restarts
% sample runs (M9); this 1D constraint set is arc-consistent, so no
% dead end is reachable.
%
% Bias rules need a LINEAR trigger (a persistent-conclusion $-rule
% Zeno-loops): `guard C C'` tokens, one per ORDERED adjacent pair, are
% spent when the C-side collapses. The symmetric pair covers both
% collapse orders; a guard whose forbid never fires is honest residue.

% ── sorts and members ──
pos: sort.
c0: pos.
c1: pos.
c2: pos.
c3: pos.

tile_t: sort.
sea: tile_t @w 2.
coast: tile_t @w 1.
land: tile_t @w 2.

% ── predicates ──
mk: (c: pos) -> type.
tile: (c: pos) -> (t: tile_t) -> type.
guard: (a: pos) -> (b: pos) -> type.
forbid: (a: tile_t) -> (b: tile_t) -> type.
bias: (x: tile_t) -> (c: tile_t) -> (w: q) -> type.

% ── the constraint: sea and land never adjacent (symmetric) ──
forbid/sl: forbid sea land.
forbid/ls: forbid land sea.

% ── the wave: one ∃_ρ per cell ──
spawn: mk C -o { exists T: tile_t @w. tile C T }.

% ── propagation = bias derivation ──
% When C's tile is ground and forbids T' next door, bias the neighbor's
% wave evar X to zero. Until C collapses, `!forbid T T'` fails on the
% evar (no fact matches an opaque unknown) and the guard waits.
constrain: guard C C' * $tile C T * !forbid T T' * $tile C' X
  -o { !bias X T' 0 }.

% ── entry (the shell's initial state; plain settle only SUSPENDS —
%    the D4 inertness pin: no tile is ever ground without the driver) ──
#expect_not_contradiction (settle: 0)
  mk c0 * mk c1 * mk c2 * mk c3
  * guard c0 c1 * guard c1 c0
  * guard c1 c2 * guard c2 c1
  * guard c2 c3 * guard c3 c2
  =>
  tile c0 sea .
